# Everything in this directory is a live credential. Nothing here is ever committed.
#
# The operator token is shell access to the host that runs Latch -- it gates /api and /mcp, and an
# approved action can run commands. A token in git history stays reachable by hash after the file is
# deleted, so the only reliable moment to stop it is before the first `git add`.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit this file alone. `*` on its own would also exclude .gitignore, which
# would leave the directory untracked entirely and the protection invisible to the next clone.
*
!.gitignore
